    <h3 id=3D"DataAnalysis:Parentfirm&amp;user-ActiveFirmdata">Active Firm =
data&nbsp;</h3>
    <p>Definition: Active firms are firms that are onboarded to Firm360 and=
 kept active. IMPORTANT: Not all Active firms are enabled in CX.</p>
    <p>Source file folder in SharePoint:&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" hr=
ef=3D"https://cbncnbccs.sharepoint.com/:f:/r/sites/Compass-X/Shared%20Docum=
ents/Product%20Management/Multi-Firm%20Users?csf=3D1&amp;web=3D1&amp;e=3DNV=
kZBg" rel=3D"nofollow">NBIN Product Team &gt; Product Management &gt; Multi=
-Firm Users</a></p>
    <p>Collection method: The source file is the Firm360 data extract (PROD=
) delivered on Mar 12, 2026</p>
    <p><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;"><em>takeaway: how many parent firms a=
re actually there?</em></span></p>
    <ul style=3D"list-style-type: square;">
     <li data-uuid=3D"fc8d6ed3-2df8-4840-8de2-73bf6cf78e8b">set up in F360&=
nbsp;</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"db9e2dde-45d2-4225-8d5e-4e3de1a30053">by the R2 id, t=
hey have cross-firm rr code assignments - interpret the firm ids the rr cod=
es are driven from&nbsp;</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>In a glance</strong></p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 91.3546%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 28.07%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 20.1719%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 51.7349%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Result</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">Total number of Active fir=
ms</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">440</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"6d7284f9-52da-4495-9497-641e84921faa">Only activ=
e firms are counted: filter rows where <code>Status_ID =3D 1</code>.</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"4f532ec2-7540-44fd-b75a-646c4eaca055">Because th=
e data extract&nbsp;has<strong> </strong>multiple rows per firm (e.g., mult=
iple RR/Account ranges per same <code>FIRMID</code>), only<strong> </strong=
>distinct <code>FIRMID</code> per <code>Parent_ID</code>, not raw rows are =
counted.</li>
         </ul>
         <p>IMPORTANT: It does not imply that all firms are "enabled" in CX=
</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th scope=3D"row" class=3D"confluenceTh">Number of Parent firms</th=
>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">85</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"5841ea16-aa54-43d4-b96f-946e3d2c07cc">NBIN Inter=
nal firms (COR) is excluded</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"53676cd4-2255-4edd-b5ad-87760eb07902">Only <code=
 style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Parent_ID</code><span style=3D"letter-spa=
cing: 0.0px;">s tied to </span><strong style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">2+<=
/strong><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"> firms are counted</span></l=
i>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTh">Min/Max number of child firms per Parent firm</th>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <p>Min: 2</p>
         <p>Max: 5</p></td>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"344beea5-e45e-4f9c-af04-cf645afd5889">Harbourfro=
nt has 5 child firms</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"c7e850fa-7abd-40e5-aa8d-040287fbe387">Worth to m=
ention that there are 4 parent firms each has 4 child firms:=20
           <ul>
            <li data-uuid=3D"6acf3193-2b6b-4970-9b6b-ea5e9a923cfb">1832 Ass=
et Mgmt (WATER)</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"5658a866-2f5d-41ca-a640-c58fdfe9cfde">BCV Asse=
t Management</li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"5ce86420-d7e3-473d-978a-167c7f8e832e"><span st=
yle=3D"color:#333333;">Bridgeport Asset Management</span></li>
            <li data-uuid=3D"bc915dbd-1295-4501-ac0e-eeafc2e25671">Cumberla=
nd</li>
           </ul></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTh">Normal count of child firms per Parent firm</th>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <p>2</p>
         <p>Percentage of parent firms in this range: 80%</p></td>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"172bd1b8-fb18-445a-82e8-9ac1a39661d2">
           <p>65 parents (80%) have 2 firms</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"fac8b3bc-4ae3-438a-a2ec-5333113ec716">
           <p>11 parents (14%) have 3 firms</p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"bfa9253e-cf89-4584-aca9-dab9d7e68c99">
           <p>4<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"> parents (5%) have </=
span>4<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"> firms</span></p></li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"42fd148f-c2d3-4675-b0ac-08154d2a30f7">
           <p>1<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"> parent (1%) has </sp=
an>5<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"> firms</span></p></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTh">Total number of child firms collectively</th>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <p>184</p></td>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <p><br></p></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h3 id=3D"DataAnalysis:Parentfirm&amp;user-Parentfirmusers">Parent firm=
 users</h3>
    <p>Assumption: A CX user is considered as a parent firm user if the fol=
lowing conditions are met:</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ea480880-eaf8-4f52-b124-860c2e47f234">User's email ad=
dress is duplicated in multiple user accounts</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"35ae25b5-d150-42ee-85c5-d92658b451cd">User's firm id =
is associated to a parent id (which is tied to 2+ firm ids)</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"9b32ea53-8324-4dd0-977e-b9d049d8a3fa">What conditions=
 are NOT considered as a factor of parent firm users?=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"6fc66085-98d2-413e-8e5e-ab73876d8281">"User's first=
 name and last name match that of another user account": This is not a good=
 condition because first name + last name are constituted to the user id, h=
ence, there is almost no chance the combination of two rows would be the sa=
me</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"b20829de-f5d8-41c7-b903-123051b101ba">"User's firm =
id is not associated to a parent id with multiple child firms": These users=
 may have multiple user accounts within their firm for various reasons, e.g=
. perform different job function or segregate client account access, but th=
ey are not considered as parent firm users</li>
       <li data-uuid=3D"04be83d2-3bd1-416c-a41a-f62acf55cfb0">"All rows wit=
h the same email address have the same firm id": Like the above, these user=
s may simply have a duplicated user account under the same firm id</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Data Deviation: As there is not a standard way to configure parent f=
irm user access in CX, there are scenarios that the above assumption may mi=
ss:&nbsp;</p>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"6d0a2def-7aea-4630-817b-9c1a01281742">User's email ad=
dresses are different in their duplicated user accounts</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"bcb31b33-1351-4f39-960b-f8af25874c5a">User's firm id =
is not associated to a parent id, which may be stemmed from data input issu=
e at Firm360</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Source file folder in SharePoint:&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" hr=
ef=3D"https://cbncnbccs.sharepoint.com/:f:/r/sites/Compass-X/Shared%20Docum=
ents/Product%20Management/Multi-Firm%20Users?csf=3D1&amp;web=3D1&amp;e=3DNV=
kZBg" rel=3D"nofollow">NBIN Product Team &gt; Product Management &gt; Multi=
-Firm Users</a></p>
    <p>Evaluation method: Join the Firm360 data extract and the CX user ext=
ract by all firms (dated March 17)</p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><strong>In a glance</strong></p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width=
: 99.9571%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 34.2581%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 18.4432%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 47.2782%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Result</th>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Total number of user rows with duplicate=
d email address</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>608</p>
         <p>For context: there are totally 9,038 rows of client user accoun=
ts</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"83bd9424-2796-46a0-aeb1-05e548c38ac5">User's ema=
il address are duplicated and their user accounts are from different firms<=
/li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d373c911-7fba-4b02-98ec-cdeeb5631e97">User's fir=
m is associated to a parent group (which is tied to 2+ firms)</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Number of users with unique email addres=
s</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">292</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"892006fb-cf82-4c3f-a859-154e41619882">Roughly sp=
eaking, there are 292 parent firm users (person)</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"32fa5837-7cfc-41a6-b480-400f4fb2255c"><em><span =
style=3D"color:#c9372c;">takeaway: the number may be higher if we count the=
 R2 misused case</span></em></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Number of distinct firm ids the users ar=
e from</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">73</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">number of child firms</td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Number of parent firms the users are fro=
m</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;"><strong>3=
4</strong></span></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">They are considered as "true" parent fir=
m users</td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Number of parent firms NO parent firm us=
er has been set up&nbsp;</th>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">47</span></p>
         <p><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">(=3D81 - 34)&nbsp;</span></p></t=
d>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"360b0731-a6d1-4760-a7d3-ca963925cc1d">Assuming a=
ll 81 parent firms are enabled in CX, only 34 firms have parent firm users =
set up, that is, 58% of parent firms do NOT have any parent firm users</li>
          <li style=3D"font-style: italic;color:#c9372c;" data-uuid=3D"70c4=
318f-0c74-44fd-af34-62aad27aa995"><em><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">takeaw=
ay: </span></em>
           <ul>
            <li style=3D"font-style: italic;color:#c9372c;" data-uuid=3D"d9=
2c53f0-5b47-40ae-9193-43b364d8d624"><em><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">who =
are the parent firms NOT having a parent firm user, why not? what are the f=
irm types bundles look like? Is there a pattern?</span></em></li>
            <li style=3D"font-style: italic;color:#c9372c;" data-uuid=3D"07=
7ade3a-d351-4854-9a77-f114e677aad5"><em><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;"> Is =
there a use case? is there a current workaround? do they limit themselves f=
or not knowing better how to use the platform?&nbsp;</span></em></li>
           </ul></li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTh">Normal duplication group size</th>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <p>2 or 3</p></td>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"ceb34d6e-fc87-4726-b628-3c45a2920360">536 rows o=
r 268 users (92%) have 2 user accounts under different firm ids</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"869fcb30-1ed0-49bc-b54d-b3f2b7bb8956">72 rows or=
 24 users (8%) have 3 user accounts under different firm ids</li>
         </ul></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <th style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTh">Parent group with the most Parent firm users</th>
        <td style=3D"text-align: left;vertical-align: top;" class=3D"conflu=
enceTd">
         <p>(Top 5)</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"46b75383-456d-459a-86b7-017f48fd6b49">Harbourfro=
nt</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"1b275f2f-1049-4954-a884-94a3f0a6a941">BCV Asset =
Management</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"db274f86-f154-4959-962e-739a911ed8c9"><span styl=
e=3D"color:#333333;">CWB McLean &amp; Partners Wealth Management</span></li=
>
          <li data-uuid=3D"b3444e65-33c8-4587-ba5f-58e7c0d9581f"><span styl=
e=3D"color:#333333;">Optimize Wealth Management</span></li>
